From f41e19c87b11dec0945b33b279279de2f4b62ec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:04:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: a draw's time on the GPU thread by part, and the
 thread's waits (measuring)

04.83's console test made the GPU thread split slower, and the single GPU
thread's profile outdoors in Breath of the Wild is flat (no function over
3.6%). So this times each part of a draw instead (common/ps4_perf.h,
DrawLap: one TSC read at each boundary, on the GPU thread only):

- RasterizerVulkan::PrepareDraw: flush, pipeline lookup, the cache
  locks, dynamic state, record, TickWork.
- GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureImpl: descriptors, image views, texture
  buffers, vertex/index, uniforms, image descriptors, render targets,
  descriptor set.

Also counted on the GPU thread:

- Waits for all the GPU's work (FenceManager::WaitPendingFences(true)),
  by what asked: the puller's fence acquire or a semaphore acquire.
- Waits for a GPU tick (Scheduler::Wait) or the Vulkan worker
  (WaitWorker).
- mprotect calls (HostMemory::Protect's arena invalidation).

The launcher's 30 s line reports them. No behaviour changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7Cki1YqWbFL1ncEV7C
